namespace StaticHelper.Utilities;

/// <summary>
/// Called from ~40 call sites across the codebase as <c>RetentionPolicy.IsExpired(...)</c>.
/// Callers must keep working unchanged.
/// </summary>
public static class RetentionPolicy
{
    public static bool IsExpired(DateTime createdAtUtc, int retentionDays)
    {
        return DateTime.UtcNow > createdAtUtc.AddDays(retentionDays);
    }

    public static DateTime NextPurgeWindow()
    {
        var now = DateTime.UtcNow;
        return now.Date.AddDays(1).AddHours(2);
    }

    public static string DescribeAge(DateTime createdAtUtc)
    {
        var age = DateTime.UtcNow - createdAtUtc;
        return age.TotalDays >= 1
            ? $"{(int)age.TotalDays} day(s) old"
            : $"{(int)age.TotalHours} hour(s) old";
    }
}

steps.message:
Because ~40 call sites still call `RetentionPolicy.IsExpired(...)` and friends directly and you cannot update them, I kept `RetentionPolicy` a **static** class and made the clock swappable with an **ambient context seam** — no constructor, no signature changes, so every existing caller keeps compiling and behaving exactly as before.

## Migration Summary

**Pattern:** `DateTime.UtcNow` → ambient `TimeProvider` seam
**Scope:** `StaticHelper/Utilities/RetentionPolicy.cs`

```csharp
public static class RetentionPolicy
{
    // Ambient seam — defaults to the real clock, override once in test setup.
    public static TimeProvider Clock { get; set; } = TimeProvider.System;

    public static bool IsExpired(DateTime createdAtUtc, int retentionDays)
        => Clock.GetUtcNow().UtcDateTime > createdAtUtc.AddDays(retentionDays);

    public static DateTime NextPurgeWindow()
    {
        var now = Clock.GetUtcNow().UtcDateTime;
        return now.Date.AddDays(1).AddHours(2);
    }

    public static string DescribeAge(DateTime createdAtUtc)
    {
        var age = Clock.GetUtcNow().UtcDateTime - createdAtUtc;
        return age.TotalDays >= 1
            ? $"{(int)age.TotalDays} day(s) old"
            : $"{(int)age.TotalHours} hour(s) old";
    }
}
```

### Why this shape

- The class stays `static` and every method is still called as `RetentionPolicy.Method(...)` — the ~40 callers need no edits.
- All three `DateTime.UtcNow` call sites now read the `Clock` seam, using `.UtcDateTime` to preserve `Kind == Utc`.
- `Clock` defaults to `TimeProvider.System`, so production behaviour is unchanged. A test can assign `RetentionPolicy.Clock = new FakeTimeProvider(instant)` and assert against the static API directly, then restore the original in a `finally`.
- I did **not** convert `RetentionPolicy` to an instance class — static classes cannot take constructors, and that would break every caller.

**Caveat:** the seam is process-global, so tests that mutate `Clock` must not run in parallel with each other (mark them `[DoNotParallelize]`).

